.TH GPU-SWITCHER 1 "@DATE@" "gpu-switcher @VERSION@" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
gpu-switcher \- switch the primary display adapter (GNOME/Mutter)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpu-switcher
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpu-switcher
is a small GTK 4 GUI application for machines with more than one GPU. It picks
which GPU the GNOME compositor (Mutter) uses as the
.B primary
display adapter by managing the udev rule
.B /etc/udev/rules.d/61-mutter-primary-gpu.rules
and activates the change with a reboot or a logout.
.PP
Pick a GPU in the list and press
.B Apply
to write the rule for it, or press
.B "Reset to auto"
to remove the rule and let Mutter choose again. The action buttons work only in
a supported GNOME/Wayland session; in any other session the app shows a warning
banner and changes nothing.
.PP
Every operation is authorized by polkit (action
.BR com.github.wl04.gpu_switcher.set-primary ,
administrator authentication, not cached: a call that succeeded a moment ago is
authorized again). The helper then writes the rule and udev is reloaded and
re-triggered
.RB ( udevadm " control \-\-reload-rules" ,
.BR "udevadm trigger" ,
.BR "udevadm info" ),
so the primary tag appears on the card without waiting for a reboot. The
display layout itself settles after the reboot or the logout the app offers.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/udev/rules.d/61-mutter-primary-gpu.rules
The managed udev rule. Before a write replaces it, the contents it replaces are
copied to
.BI rule ".bak.\fIUTC-timestamp\fR.\fIrandom-suffix\fR"
(for example
.BR 61-mutter-primary-gpu.rules.bak.20260301T120000Z.a1b2c3 ,
the five newest backups are kept).
.B "apt remove"
leaves the rule and its backups in place: they record the user's choice, not
package data. To undo the change completely, delete the rule, run
.BR "udevadm control \-\-reload-rules" ,
then log out.
.SH HELPER
The rule is written by a root helper: the systemd unit
.B gpu-switcher-helper.service
with the D-Bus name
.BR com.github.wl04.gpu_switcher.Helper .
dbus-daemon starts it on demand and it exits once it has been idle. Its sandbox
permits writes only to
.BR /etc/udev/rules.d ,
so the app itself never holds privileged access. The helper's log is read with
.HP
.B "journalctl \-u gpu-switcher-helper.service"
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
What udev actually applied to a card:
.HP
.B "udevadm info /sys/dev/dri/card1 | grep CURRENT_TAGS"
.PP
The tag
.B mutter-device-preferred-primary
on the chosen card is what Mutter reads. If it is missing, the rule is not on
disk, udev was not reloaded, or
.B "udevadm verify"
rejected the rule.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report problems at
.UR https://github.com/wl04/gpu-switcher
.UE ,
include the installed version
.RB ( "dpkg-query \-W gpu-switcher" ) ,
the GPU list
.RB ( "lspci \-nn" )
and the last lines of
.BR "journalctl \-u gpu-switcher-helper.service" .
.SH AUTHORS
Written by wl04.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR udevadm (8),
.BR lspci (8)
